<title>USA: FirstFederal Financial Q3 charge drops net.</title>
<headline>FirstFederal Financial Q3 charge drops net.</headline>
<dateline>WOOSTER, Ohio 1996-10-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.10		    $0.55</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.14		     0.43</p>
<p> Net			    782		    2,273</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.53		    $1.72</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 1.21		     1.32</p>
<p> Net			  6,685		    7,026</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is FirstFederal Financial Services Corp.  </p>
<p>1996 Q3 charge of $0.39 a share from SAIF assessment related to deposit insurance.</p>
<p>Q3 net interest income: $6.5 million vs $5.8 million.</p>
<p>Nine month net interest income: $19.2 million vs $17.9 million.</p>
<p>1996 results include non interest income of $2.6 million and $5.9 million in the Q3 and nine month periods, respectively, from manufacturered housing brokerage fees.</p>
<p>Total assets at Sept 30, 1996: $1.11 billion.</p>
<p>Total loans at Sept 30, 1996: $808.0 million.</p>
<p>Total deposits at Sept 30, 1996: $638.4 million.</p>
</text>
